## Standalone benchmark implementation prompt

[[Resources/Coder Prompts/benchmark-runner]] is the current parallel, human-judged execution/export handoff, implemented as development tooling in our AI4Research branch of JiuwenSwarm. Its runtime uses owned targets/directories and never overwrites user files. This supersedes the separate-repository interpretation; existing M1 client contracts guide integration and M2 VM/factory work is not a prerequisite.

## Optional Spark deployment prompt

[[Resources/Coder Prompts/spark-benchmark-setup]] sets up the existing app and runner directly on the Spark using Compose. It owns host preparation, storage controls and deployment connectivity. Benchmark scheduling/results remain in [[Resources/Coder Prompts/benchmark-runner]], which can run on another host. M2 VM/factory architecture below remains separate.

## Your new design work

- [[Designs/cc-containerization-and-lab-isolation|Lab boundaries and CC containerization]] separates the infrastructure prototype from the CC packaging decision.
- [[Designs/skills-to-cc-mapping|Skills to CC mapping]] defines conversion and evaluation work, including Spec Kit as a capability hypothesis.
- [[Workstreams/Workload Characterization]] retains the open hardware-design question.

Use [[Templates/Design]] for new proposals. Promote accepted product/interface changes into the maintained package through the project process.

